# Overheard talk (V2-31): two people talking near Mano, in small grey italics bottom left; it
# never takes the controls (scripts/story/overheard.gd). Each cue is one loop between the two NPCs data/world.json
# "overheard" names (a and b): a loop starts when Mano is within its radius (6 m) with a line of sight to them,
# and fades out if he walks away. `crowd` lines go to whichever of the two is a crowd member. Some carry soft
# clues. Lines only: no choices, no commands. [slot]: a line written in a friend's own
# voice, which the friend reviewed.

# Chapter 1, cour Pasteur by Amphi 4's door, after the pastry war: the report that comes back in chapter 3
~ over.ian_silvia_report
ian: The report. I'll do my half tonight. Promise. [slot]
silvia: Your half is the introduction. One paragraph. [slot]
ian: A very important paragraph. [slot]
silvia: Ian. Right now it's lorem ipsum. [slot]
ian: It's called a placeholder. It's a technique. [slot]

# Chapter 1, Amphi 4: M. Bernard at the board and the SUP asleep in the back (the side story "Segmentation fault")
~ over.prof_sleeper
prof: ...and that is why Dijkstra never slept through a lecture.
sleeper: zzz... shortest path... to bed... zzz
prof: Our friend in the back has a soutenance at 19:00.
prof: Somebody wake him. Not me. I have principles.
sleeper: zzz... core dumped... zzz

# KB1's lobby, by the round sofa
~ over.lobby_pair
crowd: Who booked SM15 and left it empty all day?
crowd: Nobody. It's haunted. By the 8:00 TP.
crowd: I'd swap my 8:00 for anything. Even a croissant.
crowd: There's literally an ad on the board saying that.

# cour Pasteur, the group by the birches
~ over.court_pair
% crowd: The moulinette gave me -42 on exercise three. Again.
% crowd: My exercise compiled first try. I don't trust it.
crowd: -42 isn't a grade. It's a warning.
if night()
	crowd: Are you staying for the BDE party?
	crowd: I'm staying for the free chips. Same thing.
else
	crowd: The hackathon poster says free pizza. I'm in.
	crowd: You're in for the pizza. Admit it.

# Chapter 2, the Under, before Karim admits anything: the "free AirPod" (a soft clue)
~ over.karim_flex
karim: Found a free AirPod this afternoon. Finders keepers.
crowd: It's one AirPod, Karim.
karim: One free AirPod. Still free.
crowd: You can't even listen in stereo.
karim: I listen to victory. In mono.

# Chapter 2, the Under, by the babyfoot
~ over.karim_joaquin
joaquin: Rematch. After you lose to Mano. [slot]
karim: Nobody beats me at my own table.
joaquin: Four defeats. Four data points. The model is converging. [slot]
karim: Converge somewhere else. I'm warming up.

~ over.ian_silvia_under
silvia: Ten euros says Karim cheats. [slot]
ian: He doesn't cheat. He's just loud. [slot]
silvia: Loud is a strategy. [slot]
ian: Then you're a grandmaster. [slot]

# Chapter 2, the cafeteria, before the coffee (a soft clue: find Mme Dupont)
~ over.madame_machine
madame: Come on. Come ON. It took my coins again.
crowd: She's been at that machine since lunch.
madame: I heard that.
crowd: Sorry, Mme Dupont. Since lunch, Mme Dupont.

# The Under, the pair at the blue table
~ over.under_pair
crowd: Who left a chip in the sofa?
crowd: That chip has been there since the WEI.
crowd: It's not a chip anymore. It's a fossil.
if night()
	crowd: The sound check is so loud my code compiled faster.
	crowd: That's not how compiling works. Keep going.
else
	crowd: Don't touch it. It's BDE heritage.

# Chapter 3, the cafeteria, before the pastry summit (the report, again)
~ over.ian_silvia_cafe
ian: Can you pass the napkins? [slot]
silvia: Can you write your half of the report? [slot]
ian: That's not a napkin. [slot]
silvia: It's not a report either. [slot]

# Chapters 3 and 4, the steps after Ishita's tour: the fairy lights
~ over.toma_ishita_lights
ishita: Left a bit. No, your left. [slot]
toma: My left is your right. This is a democracy. [slot]
ishita: Then the lights vote left. [slot]
toma: Fine. Left. Don't tell Mano I listened. [slot]

# Chapter 4, the Under: the BDE's sound check
~ over.karim_chloe_check
karim: One, two. One, two. Is this thing on?
chloe: It's been on since 20:00, Karim.
karim: Then why is nobody dancing?
chloe: Because it's a sound check.
karim: Sound checks deserve dancing.
